From 8509ade0ff6977ff213bfed9416c1a4a73000813 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:19:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [AdaptiveStream] Fix seeks at exact time boundaries and at a
 pending quality change

- A seek compares the segment and chapter starts in whole microseconds,
  rounded down as the PTS offsets of the streams. The seek time in
  microseconds converted to timescale ticks fell before a segment start
  between two microseconds (for example at a 90 kHz timescale), and the
  chapter starts summed in double precision fell after the seek time, so the
  seek continued in the segment or chapter before.
- CSession::CheckChange waits until no reader of an enabled stream reads
  asynchronously, and only then reads the state that the reader thread
  writes. m_changed and m_oldRepresentationEnded are atomic.
- A seek at a pending change of the representation always restarts the
  segment, also inside the current segment. Before, the next read returned
  data of the new representation into the reader of the old one. The reopen
  uses the buffer number of the change only while the buffers have data, so
  a seek to the first segment no longer continues at the segment of the
  change.
- start_stream allocates the segment buffers under mutex_dl_, the lock of the
  download worker, which reads the buffer list.
- The test deletes the stream before the tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
